GOAL (Product):
Add a “ChatGPT-like” intelligence layer to the existing app WITHOUT changing the existing UI layout/screens/structure.
We will ADD an in-app chat window (bottom sheet/modal) that behaves like a domain-specific ChatGPT limited to the user’s personal health/nutrition/training data.
The assistant must:
1) Read HealthKit-derived metrics + app logs (meals, workouts, recovery, protocol).
2) React to events (unexpected activity, high workday load, missed soccer, missed training).
3) Propose changes (nutrition targets, recipes, weekly plan, soccer reschedule, add/remove sessions).
4) Execute changes in the local DB ONLY via structured Actions and an Executor.
5) IMPORTANT: Large plan changes (move/cancel soccer, add/remove sessions, modify week-level training load) MUST REQUIRE explicit user confirmation EVERY TIME before writing to DB.

NON-GOALS:
- Do not redesign the app UI or navigation. No new major tabs.
- No backend sync or cloud storage.
- No medical diagnosis, no medication dosage changes. User-entered schedules only.
- No “always-on background AI”. Use event triggers + user chat interactions.

HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN:
We will implement an “Agent + Tools” pattern:
- Chat UI is a bottom sheet/modal opened from existing screens via a small “Coach” button (FAB or icon button), matching current theme.
- The Agent builds a compact context bundle from local data depending on where the chat is opened (Nutrition screen context vs Workouts screen context vs Home screen context).
- The Agent calls GeminiCoachService with a strict system prompt and returns:
  (a) assistant text (concise)
  (b) optional structured Action Proposals (JSON) to modify data/plans
  (c) suggested quick replies/buttons
- The App NEVER lets the model directly write to DB.
- Instead, Action Proposals are stored locally as PendingProposals, shown to user in a “Plan Preview Card” inside the chat.
- When user taps “Approve”, the ActionExecutor validates constraints and applies DB mutations.
- Every write is logged in AuditLog (local).

