ACTION SCHEMA (Structured Outputs):
Define a strict JSON schema for ActionProposal to be generated by the model.
Store schema in code as constants and validate with json_schema or manual validation.

Top-level ActionProposal:
{
  "proposal_id": "string",
  "type": "string",
  "scope": "small|large",
  "requires_confirmation": true|false,
  "preview": { "title":"string", "summary":"string" },
  "actions": [ ActionItem... ],
  "constraints": [ "string"... ],
  "reasoning_short": [ "string"... ],
  "safe_to_auto_apply": false
}

ActionItem union types (minimum set):
A) Nutrition
- "log_meal": { mealLogId? OR create new meal + items, calories/macros estimates, confidence }
- "set_nutrition_targets": { date, calories_target, protein_g, carbs_g, fat_g, water_ml, reason }
- "suggest_recipe": { title, ingredients[], steps[], estimated_calories_range, macros, cuisineTag }
NOTE: recipe suggestion is NOT a DB write unless user approves saving it or scheduling it.

B) Events
- "add_activity_event": { type, startAt, durationMin, intensity?, source, notes? }
- "update_activity_event": { id, fields... }
- "delete_activity_event": { id } (scope=large if impacts plan)

C) Training Plan (ALL of these are scope=large and require confirmation ALWAYS)
- "reschedule_session": { planId, sessionId, fromDay, toDay }
- "add_session": { planId, dayOfWeek, sessionType, durationMin, intensity, title }
- "cancel_session": { planId, sessionId, reason }
- "modify_session": { planId, sessionId, changes... }
- "apply_plan_diff": { planId, diff: { move[], add[], cancel[], modify[] } }

VALIDATION RULES (Hard constraints):
Implement these checks in ActionExecutor (reject proposal if violated):
- Any training plan change => scope MUST be "large" and requires_confirmation MUST be true.
- Never schedule 2 high-intensity sessions back-to-back unless explicitly allowed by constraints AND user confirms.
- Respect recovery state:
  - If readiness/recovery is Red today, do not schedule high intensity today.
- Respect “soccer as high load” assumption:
  - Day after soccer defaults to recovery or low intensity.
- If user has knee pain flag in protocol constraints, avoid adding high-impact run/plyo; propose alternatives.
- No medication dosage changes. Only allow “reminder schedule logging” if already user-entered.

